      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The industry standard generally distinguishes between satire and hate speech by looking at intent and impact. Satire, even if provocative, is usually protected when it is clearly mocking a concept or public figure, rather than targeting protected characteristics. Hate speech is typically flagged when humor or commentary is used to incite violence, dehumanize, or systematically attack individuals based on attributes like race, religion, or gender. The line is drawn where the communication shifts from criticism to targeted abuse against a protected group.",
